version cpag_2025
  cite cpag_report
  governs 2025
  known 2025-10-31
  note "The report is dated only by its month, October 2025, so it is known on the month's last day (LANGUAGE §4.5). A web lookup (2026-10-19) gave no day: the PDF sits under /2025-10/ on CPAG's site, CPAG's news page for it (https://cpag.org.uk/news/cost-child-2025) refused the request (HTTP 403), and the PDF's creation stamp (2025-10-21, case transcription notes) is not a publication date. Entitlements are updated to April 2025 (p. 3, Note)."
  note "Basic cost leaves out rent, childcare and council tax (p. 3, Note); the report doesn't say what else Full cost holds."
  cpag_cost = ?"CPAG adds up the cost of each year of childhood by birth order (p. 2) but prints no yearly costs" "p. 2, Introduction; p. 3, Scorecard rows 1-2"
  cpag_min = ?"CPAG doesn't print the minimum family costs behind its percentages" "p. 3, Scorecard rows 3-5 and Note"
  cpag_net = ?"CPAG doesn't print the net incomes behind its percentages" "p. 3, Scorecard rows 3-5 and Note"

version usda_example
  cite usda_report
  governs always
  known 2026-10-18
  note "Table 10's example assumes a child born in 2015 who reaches age 17 in 2032, at 2.2 percent average annual inflation: a worked example's stipulation, known from the model's on, since it has no start (LANGUAGE §4.5)."
  infl = 0.022 1/year governs 2015..2032 "PDF p. 25: a child born in 2015 reaches age 17 in 2032, and the average annual inflation rate over this time is 2.2 percent"
